# 0008 — VIEWER MODE: /?viewer=1 opens a StarNet page that can only LOOK (e.g. for a public stream of the station)
# Status: NOT APPLIED (optional; scripts/setup-station.sh skips it by default)
# Owners: tools (the patch), risk (security review). Why: StarNet has no read-only mode: any second page pushes its
# roster and save on load, takes the away briefing, stamps presence, acks bridge verbs and is counted as an open page.
# What it changes (all inert unless the page URL carries viewer=1; the flag only ever REMOVES):
#   frontend/app/viewer.js (new) — read once from the URL, frozen; fetch/XHR allow only GET/HEAD (local 403
#     X-StarNet-Code: viewer_readonly), sendBeacon sends nothing, localStorage/sessionStorage writes stay in memory, no
#     BroadcastChannel traffic or page lock, the feed is marked viewer=1, private surfaces and the camera frame's activity
#     ticker are not drawn, badge.
#   frontend/index.html — loads it right after bootguard.js, ahead of every script that fetches, stores or broadcasts.
#   frontend/app/stationcommands.js — a viewer runs no bridge verb (one early return); website/app/app/stationcommands.js
#     gets the same line (test/orchestration.test.js keeps that mirror byte-identical).
#   sidecar/index.js — a viewer=1 feed is never counted as an open page (ssePages), and its reply says X-StarNet-Viewer: 1.
# Tests: node company/tools/tests/viewer-mode.e2e.js --starnet <tree with this applied> (zero non-GET requests,
#   workspace and save unchanged, feed marked); the control page without the flag writes.
# Apply (after 0001-0007, from the project root), then restart the station when no loop is running:
#     git -C starnet apply --3way ../company/patches/0008-viewer-mode.diff && sed -i "2s/^# Status: NOT APPLIED.*/# Status: APPLIED $(date +%F)/" company/patches/0008-viewer-mode.diff
#   If the locked-file watcher flags the StarNet change, accept each changed file from the owner's shell:
#     node company/tools/locked-watch.js accept starnet/<file> --by owner --why "patch 0008 applied"
# Revert: git -C starnet apply -R ../company/patches/0008-viewer-mode.diff && sed -i "2s/^# Status: APPLIED.*/# Status: NOT APPLIED/" company/patches/0008-viewer-mode.diff
#   then the same restart.
