+/* viewer.js — VIEWER MODE: a StarNet page that only LOOKS (Ca Phe Digital company patch 0008, company/patches/).
+
+   Open the station as http://127.0.0.1:<port>/?viewer=1 and this page shows the live floor exactly as the Commander's
+   page does, but it cannot change anything:
+     · fetch: only GET and HEAD leave the page; every other method gets a local 403 (X-StarNet-Code: viewer_readonly),
+       so the save, the roster push, settings, agent changes, runs, acks and presence stamps never reach the station;
+     · XMLHttpRequest: the same rule; navigator.sendBeacon (the unload save) sends nothing;
+     · localStorage / sessionStorage: writes land in a copy held in memory, so another StarNet tab in the same browser
+       never sees this page's journals, settings or caches (reads see that copy over the real store);
+     · BroadcastChannel and the page lock: this page neither answers nor joins the other tabs' "who else is open?";
+     · the live feed (EventSource) is marked viewer=1, so the station never counts this page as an open StarNet page
+       (sidecar/index.js handleChannelEvents), and stationcommands.js never runs a bridge verb here;
+     · private surfaces (COMMS, the session rail, notifications, windows, widget rails, the camera frame's activity
+       ticker) are not drawn, and a badge says VIEWER · READ-ONLY.
+   THE FLAG ONLY REMOVES. It is read once, from this page's own URL, before any other script, and frozen
+   (non-writable, non-configurable): nothing in a save, a setting, storage or the server can switch it on or off later.
+   Every branch on window.__STARNET_VIEWER__ elsewhere must be an early return or a refusal; a branch that adds a route,
+   a token, a control or a capability fails review. Limits: a same-origin frame (an app, a plugin window) is its own
+   page and is not covered; company/tools/station-view.js adds a network-level GET-only guard for its captures.
+   MUST be the first script in index.html. */
